      "name": "bom-prefixed",
      "why": "leading UTF-8 byte order mark. NOT a grammar violation: RFC 8259 section 8.1 permits a receiver to ignore one. That permission is the hazard — \"MAY ignore\" lets two conformant implementations disagree, and in a content-addressed format the same record then has two addresses. Measured 2026-07-30: Python accepted it, Go rejected it. Rejecting is a deliberate narrowing of the domain."
